+# Flight 93 FAA replies and the radar-disc inventory
+
+Public derivative of the November 10, 2026 source review. B129 / PD01–PD04 and REC01 / REC03 acquisition. The public FAA collection supplies two original agency responses in a released scan and a 57-file catalog for an FAA disc labeled as radar data released to NTSB. These narrow the Flight 93 records search. The join to the **2006005841** referral and its CD remains open. [FAA replies, NAID 7597314](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/7597314) · [FAA disc finding aid](https://www.archives.gov/research/foia/faa-finding-aid-96-107#:~:text=Radar%20Data%20Released%20to%20NTSB) · [2006 referral, physical p. 435](https://www.governmentattic.org/docs/FOIA_Logs_FAA_FY2006.pdf#page=435)
+
+## Original replies and later public distribution
+
+| Record | Scope and observation |
+| --- | --- |
+| FAA reply **2001-008306GL**, dated **November 5, 2001**, ZOB-188 physical pp. 3–4, p. 3 sorted lines 11 and 15–33 | A September 20 request sought the transcript of Cleveland controller communications with United 93. FAA withheld the transcript, citing the ongoing investigation and discussing Exemptions 7(A) and 7(E). |
+| FAA reply **2002-006815GL**, dated **August 9, 2002**, ZOB-188 physical pp. 1–2, p. 1 sorted lines 12 and 16–34 | A July 11 facsimile requested a rerecording of the United 93 voice communication tape. FAA withheld the tapes with a corresponding investigation rationale and exemption discussion. |
+| National Security Archive, **August 11, 2006**, Briefing Book 196, raw HTML lines 221–227, 249–263 and 401–405 | The recipient reported obtaining four ATC transcripts directly from NTSB and posted the United 93 report as Document 8. The PDF has 16 physical pages. Its cover describes certified analog copies from several facilities and an audio and text transcription process. |
+| FAA FY 2006 log **2006005841**, physical p. 435 sorted lines 20–26 | The subject describes an NTSB referral of a UA93 CD. Preserve the **August 2** logged date, **September 19** return and **October 5** assignment. The original packet and receiving records remain unacquired. |
+
+The earlier requests distinguish a Cleveland transcript from a voice-tape rerecording. The later recipient posting supplies an NTSB transcript PDF with a broader described source scope. Keep the original denials, recipient account and referral log as separate records. The held scans leave open whether the earlier Cleveland transcript, underlying tape, composite NTSB transcript and 2006 CD share particular bytes or source channels. [FAA replies PDF](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/7597314) · [Recipient posting](https://nsarchive2.gwu.edu/NSAEBB/NSAEBB196/) · [Document 8, p. 1](https://nsarchive2.gwu.edu/NSAEBB/NSAEBB196/doc08.pdf#page=1)
+
+A separate filed affidavit, **SDNY 1:08-cv-10881-DC, docket 17-5**, physical pp. 1–2, paragraphs 6–8, reports an **August 4, 2006** request concerning flight-path studies of **AA11, UA175 and AA77** and **three CD-ROMs** reportedly sent in August. It separately reports **two DVDs** with AA77 and UA93 animations following a **February 18, 2007** request. The source is a public reproduction of a filed party declaration. The actual request and delivery packet, rather than proximity in month or medium type, are required for a join to the FAA's August 2 referral. [Filed affidavit, physical p. 2](https://centerfor911justice.org/news/Filed%3D20Affidavit%3D20Balsamo.pdf#page=2)
+
+## Find the actual media by inventory number
+
+| FAA inventory | Locator and what it records |
+| --- | --- |
+| **PIT-36**, Box 19 | Inventory PDF physical p. 58 line 25 describes custody documentation for **one ZIP disk** of United 93 CDR data. The finding aid's raw HTML row starts on line 6229 and supplies no digital item or NAID for the entry. The custody document and disk remain unacquired. |
+| **AWA-709**, Box 100 | Inventory PDF p. 261 line 18 lists a **United 93 wave file** on compact disc. The HTML row at 10523 points to ten digitized files. |
+| **AWA-715**, Box 100 | Inventory PDF p. 261 line 24 and HTML row 12206 record **9/21** for the NTSB radar release, with the year unstated in those descriptions. The HTML advertises **57** digitized files. The exact folder-number count produces **57 rows and 57 distinct NAIDs**. Twelve have United 93 catalog titles. |
+| **AEA#861**, Box 102 | Inventory PDF p. 264 line 26 describes Pittsburgh United 93 CDR radar data with **13:30:02–14:30:09 UTC**. The entry describes a compact disc. Keep it separate from the Pittsburgh ZIP disk and the AWA-715 Pittsburgh file. |
+
+The twelve United 93 AWA-715 rows occupy raw HTML lines **12323–12422** at nine-line intervals. These include **PIT UAL93.txt** (NAID **7596916**) and eleven ZOB-ARTCC-287 entries. The first A group lists beacon and info. B, C and D each list beacon, info and primary. The scoped list leaves the status of an A-group primary file open. We acquired **7596923**, the **26-byte** C-group information object. Its lines are `001,134400`, `001,140000` and `zob`. Their meaning requires the original format and transfer records. The exact folder count describes the catalog listing, with native disc contents and completeness unresolved. [Accession inventory, p. 58](https://www.archives.gov/files/faa-inventory.pdf#page=58) · [Inventory, p. 261](https://www.archives.gov/files/faa-inventory.pdf#page=261) · [Boxes 12–23 finding aid](https://www.archives.gov/research/foia/faa-finding-aid-12-23) · [Boxes 96–107 finding aid](https://www.archives.gov/research/foia/faa-finding-aid-96-107) · [Pittsburgh file](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/7596916) · [C-group info file](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/7596923)
+
+## Preserve identifiers and scope
+
+- The NTSB transcript cover, physical p. 1, reads **DCA01SA065**. The NTSB's one-item docket, project **53530**, reads **DCA01MA065**. The separate one-page Information Document assigns control of generated material to the FBI and says the Board did not plan to open a public docket. Preserve the stated plan alongside the current one-item listing. The cover and docket agree on United 93, Shanksville, September 11, 2001 and a Boeing 757. A docket crosswalk or transmittal using both identifiers could establish their administrative relationship. [NTSB transcript](https://nsarchive2.gwu.edu/NSAEBB/NSAEBB196/doc08.pdf#page=1) · [NTSB docket](https://data.ntsb.gov/Docket?ProjectID=53530) · [Information Document](https://data.ntsb.gov/Docket/Document/docBLOB?FileExtension=.PDF&FileName=Information+Document-Master.PDF&ID=40256405)
+- The August 11 posting reports release of Flight 93 material. The FAA's earlier written withholding decisions had specifically described ongoing investigative circumstances. A later release of an NTSB product leaves the eventual disposition of each earlier FAA request open. The separate FAA 2006 referral still requires the original CD label, copy directory and handoff records.
+
+## Verification and open inputs
+
+November 10 UTC access. Nine saved response bodies verified against acquisition hashes. The newly downloaded Document 8 matches the earlier source pin byte for byte. The scoped verification checked catalog-object bindings, the digitized-row census, twelve UA93 locators, selected letter and affidavit passages and the exact bytes of one small info object. Both FAA reply date stamps and the NTSB cover number were read from the page images. Raw scans and requester details are retained locally. The report carries source links and a narrow reading of the relevant fields.
+
+- [ ] **PD01 / REC01 / REC03.** Obtain the original 2006005841 NTSB-to-FAA cover and disc manifest, FAA return and NTSB receipt, and any relation to the GWU publication. Seek the actual PIT-36 custody document, AWA-715 release cover including year and receipt, and the listed Pittsburgh radar file's source chain.
+- [ ] **PD01 / REC03.** Seek the original FAA requests, any appeal or later final dispositions for **2001-008306GL** and **2002-006815GL**, and the NTSB recording/transcript source inventory. Audio and clock comparisons remain with the technical workstream.
+- [ ] **PD01–PD04.** Keep the FAA corrected May 2003 answer and dated delivery, signed action/no-action decision, recommendation-specific disposition and governing case procedure open. This acquisition concerns the release and custody of operational records. [Case queue](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/055ef54a857b46846d0038109bab7e108970f03a/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-postreport-disposition-2026-10-27/README.md)
